INT. ROLLER DERBY RINK - BASEMENT OF A BOWLING ALLEY - NIGHT

Cracked maple floor. Bleachers made of old pews. A hand-painted banner reads: THE DOCKSIDE DAMES.

Two skaters sit on a bench, lacing up. The younger, PRISCILLA "PRISS" MONTEIRO (20s, shaved head, neon wrist guards), bounces a knee. The older, COACH ARLETTE BEAUMONT-WEI (50s, clipboard, whistle, a voice like gravel), stands over her.

ARLETTE
Eyes up. Head up. Heart up.

PRISS
Which one first?

ARLETTE
All of them.

She blows the whistle. It echoes off the pews.

PRISS
(muttering)
Okay. Okay. Okay.

ARLETTE
(to the empty room)
Anybody else? Anybody?

Silence. A single pew creaks.

ARLETTE (CONT'D)
(louder, to Priss)
Where's the rest of the team?

PRISS
Flu. Four of them. And Dana's cousin's wedding.

ARLETTE
We have a bout in twenty minutes.

PRISS
I know.

ARLETTE
With three skaters.

PRISS
Two. You don't skate.

Arlette glares. Priss shrinks.

The basement door bangs. A stranger descends the steps: a woman in a long coat and rental skates, rolling unsteadily down the aisle. RESERVE SKATER (30s, athletic, bleached ponytail, a duffel on her shoulder). She stops at the rail.

RESERVE SKATER
Is this the Dockside Dames?

ARLETTE
Who's asking?

RESERVE SKATER
Somebody who played four years for the Harbor Hellcats.

PRISS
(whisper)
She's a Hellcat.

ARLETTE
(to Priss)
I can hear.

RESERVE SKATER
I got cut. Long story. I need a team.

ARLETTE
We need a body.

RESERVE SKATER
I'm more than a body.

ARLETTE
What's your name?

RESERVE SKATER
Odalys. Odalys Ferreira.

ARLETTE
Welcome, Odalys.

Odalys drops her duffel and sits. Priss scoots over.

PRISS
(to Odalys)
You're really a Hellcat?

ODALYS
Was.

ARLETTE
(to the room)
Three skaters. Nobody's tired. Nobody's hurt. Nobody's quitting.

PRISS
Nobody's even stretched.

ARLETTE
Stretch on the track.

She blows the whistle. The three of them stand, wobble, roll toward the rink. Odalys glances back at the empty pews and mutters.

ODALYS
(to herself)
Please let somebody come.
